-- title:
--   Existence of a twisted fibre datum from annulus data
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $p$ is a prime and $M$ a positive integer with $p \mid M$ (`hpM`) and $p^{2} \nmid M$ (`hpM2`), and $H \le (\mathbb Z/M)^{\times}$ is a subgroup containing every unit whose image under `ZMod.unitsMap` along $M/p \mid M$ is $1$ (`hHp`). Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`), and its residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Write $F_M =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` and $F_{M/p} =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (M/p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` for the base-changed modular function fields over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $\bar F =$ `Fbar p M H hpM κ`, the $q$-expansion function field over $\kappa$ of the group `ΓN p M H hpM`.
--
--   The degeneracy data are: an automorphism $\theta$ of $F_M$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; an integral $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra map $\alpha : F_{M/p} \to F_M$ (`hα`), such that the composite $\beta =$ ($\alpha$ followed by $\theta$) is integral as well (`hβ`); the hypothesis `hα_coe`, that $\alpha$ is the identity on underlying Laurent series, and `hβ_coe`, that $\beta$ is $q \mapsto q^{p}$ on Laurent series, i.e. composition with `qExpand _ p`. A unit $pb$ of $\mathbb Z/(M/p)$ with underlying value $p$ (`hpb`) determines a diamond automorphism of $\bar F$, namely `diamondActionModL κ (M/p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM) (CuspForm.gammaLift (M/p) pb)`, and the map $\delta$ on places of $\bar F$ over $\kappa$ is required (`hδ`) to be the action of the associated semilinear automorphism `SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut` on places. A finite set $SS$ of pairs of places of $\bar F$ is required (`hSS`) to consist exactly of the elements of `ssNodePairsQExp κ (ΓN p M H hpM) p`, that is, of the pairs $s$ with $s.2$ a supersingular place and $s.1$ its $q$-expansion Frobenius image `qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL`. Finally, $Psp$ is a place specialisation `JHPlaceSpecialization p M H hpM A`, sending places of $F_{M/p}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ to places of $\bar F$ over $\kappa$, and $Rpd$ is a `ProlongationDatum` for $Psp$ and $\theta$, consisting of two regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $\bar F$ along $A$ with the compatibilities recorded in that structure. Recall that `reduceFst` is $W \mapsto Psp.\mathrm{sp}(W|_{\alpha})$, `reduceSnd` is $W \mapsto \delta(Psp.\mathrm{sp}(W|_{\beta}))$, that $W$ is `IsStrictFst` when $\delta(\mathrm{Frob}(\mathrm{reduceFst}\,W)) = \mathrm{reduceSnd}\,W$ and $\mathrm{reduceFst}\,W$ is not $\delta$-`Fixed`, and dually for `IsStrictSnd`, `Fixed` $\delta\,v$ meaning $\mathrm{Frob}(\delta(\mathrm{Frob}\,v)) = v$.
--
--   The remaining hypotheses fall into the following groups, whose content is summarised here.
--
--   Fixed-place hypotheses: `hFix` states that every supersingular place $y$ of `ssPlacesQExp κ (ΓN p M H hpM) p` and its Frobenius image are $\delta$-`Fixed`; `hFixFin` states that the set of $\delta$-`Fixed` places of $\bar F$ is finite.
--
--   Gluing laws for the pair $(\alpha,\beta)$ and $\delta$: `hTD` is `TypeDichotomy` (every place of $F_M$ satisfies one of the two Frobenius relations between its two reductions); `hmodel` is `Rpd.IsModel` (the two divisor laws together with the two cusp laws); `hO` is `OrderLawFixed` (for $f$ lying in both rings of integers with non-zero residues, the push-forward along `reduceFst` of the divisor of $f$ at a $\delta$-fixed affine place $v$ is the sum of the order of the $R_1$-residue at $v$ and of the order of the $R_2$-residue at $\delta(\mathrm{Frob}\,v)$); `hreg` is `RegularityLaw` relative to $SS$ (positivity of the two residue orders at $\delta$-fixed affine places, and a common value at the two coordinates of each $s \in SS$); `hnv` is `NodeValueLaw` relative to $SS$ (a common non-zero value of the two residues at the coordinates of $s$, when the divisor of $f$ avoids the pair $s$).
--
--   Galois equivariance: `hθgal` states that $\theta$ commutes with the action of every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ on $F_M$ through `arithmeticGalois`.
--
--   Two local pole bounds, `hLFst` and `hLSnd`: for distinct places $Q, Q'$ of $F_M$, both `IsStrictFst` (resp. both `IsStrictSnd`) with the same, affine, reduction, for a natural number $n$ non-zero in $\kappa$, and for $g$ in the integers of $R_1$ (resp. $R_2$) with non-zero residue such that $\operatorname{ord}_Q g = -n$, $\operatorname{ord}_{Q'} g = n$ and $\operatorname{ord}_W g = 0$ for every other strict place $W$ with the same reduction, if $g = 1 + e\,\varepsilon$ with $e \in A$ and $\varepsilon$ in the integers of $R_1$ (resp. $R_2$) with non-zero residue, then the order of that residue at the common reduction of $Q$ is at least $-1$.
--
--   A unit hypothesis `hUnit`: there exist $u_1, u_2 \in F_M$ and divisors $D_1, D_2$ on $F_M$ equal to the divisors of $u_1$ and of $u_2$ respectively, such that $u_1$ and $u_1^{-1}$ lie in the integers of $R_1$ with non-zero residue of $u_1$, the push-forward along `reduceFst` of the strict-first part `fstDiv` of $D_1$ agrees at every non-$\delta$-fixed place $v$ with the order at $v$ of the $R_1$-residue of $u_1$, and the push-forward along `reduceFst` of the part of $D_1$ supported on `IsInftySide` places agrees, at the reduction of each such place $C$, with the order there of that residue; dually for $u_2$, $R_2$, `sndDiv`, `reduceSnd` and `IsZeroSide`; together with the two interchange clauses that every non-zero $f \in F_M$ admits $m \neq 0$ and $j \in \mathbb Z$ with $f^{m}u_1^{j}$ in the integers of $R_2$ (resp. $f^{m}u_2^{j}$ in the integers of $R_1$) with non-zero residue.
--
--   Cusp and orientation hypotheses: `hcusp` states that every non-`IsAffinePlace` place $w$ of $\bar F$ is the `reduceFst`-image of some `IsInftySide` place and the `reduceSnd`-image of some `IsZeroSide` place; `horientInf` states $\delta(\mathrm{Frob}(\mathrm{reduceFst}\,C)) = \mathrm{reduceSnd}\,C$ for `IsInftySide` places $C$, and `horient0` states $\mathrm{reduceFst}\,C = \mathrm{Frob}(\mathrm{reduceSnd}\,C)$ for `IsZeroSide` places $C$.
--
--   Annulus data: a function $e : SS \to \mathbb N$ with $e(s) > 0$ (`he`); the hypothesis `hAnn`, asserting for each $s \in SS$ the existence of an `Annulus` over $A$ on $F_M$ whose domain consists exactly of the places $W$ with $\mathrm{reduceFst}\,W = s.1$ which are neither `IsStrictFst` nor `IsStrictSnd`, whose modulus is $p^{e(s)}$ times a unit of $A$, whose parameter is fixed by the `arithmeticGalois` action of the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, for which $(\mathrm{modulus})^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{param}$ lies in the integers of $R_1$ and $\mathrm{param}$ lies in the integers of $R_2$ with non-zero residue, and which satisfies the two end-slope clauses: the $R_2$-residue of $\mathrm{param}$ has order $1$ at $s.2$ and, for every $f$ in the integers of $R_2$ with non-zero residue and with $\operatorname{ord}_P f = 0$ on the annulus, the element $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \cdot (P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,\mathrm{param})^{-\operatorname{ord}_{s.2}(\text{residue of } f)}$ is a unit of $A$ at every $P$ of the domain; and the mirror clause for the flipped parameter $\mathrm{modulus}\cdot\mathrm{param}^{-1}$, $R_1$ and $s.1$. A specific family $An$ of annuli satisfying exactly these conditions is given (`hAn`).
--
--   A slope hypothesis `hVSlope`: for every family of annuli satisfying the conditions just listed, and every $k \in \mathbb N$ divisible by all $e(s)$, there exist $f \neq 0$ in $F_M$ and $c \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $c\cdot f$ in the integers of $R_1$ with non-zero residue, such that the divisor of $f$ is a good divisor in the sense of `IsGoodDiv` (supported on strict places), $\operatorname{ord}_V f = 0$ for every place $V$ whose `reduceFst`-image is $\delta$-fixed and is not a coordinate $s.1$ of an element of $SS$, the residue of $c\cdot f$ has order $0$ at every $\delta$-fixed place distinct from all $s.1$, and for each $s$ there is $a \neq 0$ with $\operatorname{ord}_P f = 0$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \cdot a \cdot (P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,(An\,s).\mathrm{param})^{-(k/e(s))}$ a unit of $A$ at every $P$ in the domain of $An\,s$.
--
--   Reading and regularity hypotheses at fixed places: `hFixReadFst` and `hFixReadSnd` state that for $g$ in the integers of $R_1$ (resp. $R_2$) with non-zero residue and for a $\delta$-fixed place $v$ distinct from all $s.1$ (resp. all $s.2$), if $\operatorname{ord}_V g = 0$ for all $V$ with reduction $v$, then the residue of $g$ has order $0$ at $v$; `hFixRegFst` and `hFixRegSnd` are the corresponding statements with $v$ in addition `IsAffinePlace` and with the order inequalities $0 \le \operatorname{ord}_V g$ and $0 \le \operatorname{ord}_v(\text{residue})$.
--
--   Position data: a function $pos$ assigning to each $s \in SS$ and each place of $F_M$ a rational number, subject to `hpos`, the `AnnulusPositionLaw` for $SS$, $e$, $An$ and $pos$ (for $V$ in the domain of $An\,s$ one has $0 < pos\,s\,V < e(s)$ and the valuation identity $A.\mathrm{valuation}(V.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{modulus}\cdot\mathrm{param}^{-1}))^{\mathrm{den}} = A.\mathrm{valuation}(p)^{\mathrm{num}}$ for that rational); to `hposσ`, invariance of $pos\,s$ under the `arithmeticGalois` action of `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` on places; and to `hposD`, the existence, for each $s$ and each integer $0 < d < e(s)$, of an inertia-invariant place $V$ in the domain of $An\,s$ with $pos\,s\,V = d$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exists a twisted fibre datum $dat :$ `TwistedFibreDatum SS`, consisting of elements $\mathrm{unifFst}(s), \mathrm{unifSnd}(s) \in \bar F$, divisors $\mathrm{corrFst}(s), \mathrm{corrSnd}(s)$ on $\bar F$ over $\kappa$ and units $u_0(s), \lambda(s), \mu(s) \in \kappa^{\times}$ for $s \in SS$, satisfying the following five assertions.
--
--   First, for every $s \in SS$: the divisor $\mathrm{single}(s.1, 1) + \mathrm{corrFst}(s)$ takes at every place $v$ the value $\operatorname{ord}_v(\mathrm{unifFst}(s))$; for every $s' \in SS$ one has $\mathrm{corrFst}(s)(s'.1) = 0$ and $\mathrm{corrFst}(s)(s'.2) = 0$; and $\mathrm{corrFst}(s)$ has degree $-1$.
--
--   Second, for every $s \in SS$: the divisor $\mathrm{single}(s.2, 1) + \mathrm{corrSnd}(s)$ takes at every place $v$ the value $\operatorname{ord}_v(\mathrm{unifSnd}(s))$; for every $s' \in SS$ one has $\mathrm{corrSnd}(s)(s'.1) = 0$ and $\mathrm{corrSnd}(s)(s'.2) = 0$; and $\mathrm{corrSnd}(s)$ has degree $-1$.
--
--   Third, for every $s \in SS$ there is a unit $u$ of $A$ with $(An\,s).\mathrm{modulus} = p^{e(s)}\,u$ and $\mathrm{residue}_A(u) = u_0(s)$.
--
--   Fourth, for every $s \in SS$ and every witness that the flipped parameter `flipParam SS An s` $= (An\,s).\mathrm{modulus}\cdot(An\,s).\mathrm{param}^{-1}$ lies in the integers of $R_1$, the place $s.1$ has value $\lambda(s)$ at the quotient of the $R_1$-residue of that element by $\mathrm{unifFst}(s)$, in the sense of `HasValue`: the quotient lies in the valuation ring of $s.1$ and its residue there is the image of $\lambda(s)$ in the residue field of $s.1$.
--
--   Fifth, for every $s \in SS$ and every witness that $(An\,s).\mathrm{param}$ lies in the integers of $R_2$, the place $s.2$ has value $\mu(s)$ at the quotient of the $R_2$-residue of that parameter by $\mathrm{unifSnd}(s)$, again in the sense of `HasValue`.
--
--   This is the construction step producing, on the special fibre at $p$ of the modular curve $X_H(M)$ with $p \parallel M$, the node-by-node data of the twisted gluing: uniformisers at the two coordinates of each supersingular node pair, their correction divisors of degree $-1$ away from the nodes, and the three node constants $u_0$, $\lambda$, $\mu$ read off from the annulus moduli and parameters. It is used by the subsequent statement on inertia-fixed strict good divisors and the vanishing of the associated glued class, which consumes the datum thus obtained.
